      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea is that if a lower EL triggers an exception taken to EL3 by using some disabled CPU feature, then EL3 injects the exception back to that EL, so that the kernel/hypervisor can mitigate it in some way (avoid using the feature/terminate the VM that used it). That way a full EL3 crash can be avoided. I guess for debugging purposes it could be useful to have a way of setting it to crash.",
